// Standard-conforming <variant>, ported from LLVM libc++'s <variant>
// (runtime/toolchains/src/llvm-project/libcxx/include/variant) into namespace
// sprt and adapted to this freestanding, -fno-exceptions runtime.
//
//  * The class is built from the same layered base classes as libc++
//    (__union -> __base -> __dtor -> __ctor -> __move_constructor ->
//    __copy_constructor -> __assignment -> __move_assignment ->
//    __copy_assignment -> __impl). Each layer is generated in three flavours
//    (TriviallyAvailable / Available / Unavailable) selected by the properties
//    of the alternatives, so the special members of variant<Types...> propagate
//    the triviality of the alternatives: variant<int, float> is trivially
//    copyable / movable / destructible, etc.
//
//  * Every member is noexcept: the runtime is compiled -fno-exceptions, so an
//    alternative's operation cannot throw and there is no exceptional path to
//    propagate. The libc++ "throwing" points become defined aborts via
//    __throw_bad_variant_access() (used by get<>() on the wrong alternative).
//
//  * valueless state and variant_empty (sprt extension, kept by design):
//    a std::variant can become "valueless_by_exception" only if an exception is
//    thrown while changing the active alternative. With exceptions disabled that
//    can never happen during construction/assignment, so the only way a variant
//    becomes valueless here is the move of a variant whose alternatives are NOT
//    all trivially movable: in that (the __move_constructor/__move_assignment
//    _Available) path the moved-from source is left valueless (whereas a variant
//    of trivially-movable alternatives keeps its defaulted, trivial move and the
//    moved-from source stays engaged, so trivial-move propagation is preserved).
//    Visiting a valueless variant does not abort; instead the visitor is invoked
//    with a `variant_empty{}` in place of the (missing) alternative. This is the
//    -fno-exceptions analogue of std::visit throwing bad_variant_access, and it
//    lets a generic visitor observe "this variant was moved from". get<>() on a
//    valueless variant still aborts (a reference cannot be degraded gracefully).

